-- title:
--   Minimal polynomial and power basis from an exact monic evaluation kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, let $A$ be a commutative $K$-algebra, and let $x\in A$. Suppose that a monic polynomial $m\in K[T]$ describes the exact evaluation kernel:
--   $$
--   q(x)=0\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad m\mid q
--   \qquad(q\in K[T]).
--   $$
--   Here evaluation uses the specified $K$-algebra structure on $A$. Put $d=\deg(m)$ and let $K[x]\subseteq A$ be the subalgebra generated by $x$.
--
--   Then the minimal polynomial of $x$ over $K$ is $m$. The algebra $K[x]$ admits a power basis whose generator maps to $x$ in $A$ and whose dimension is $d$. In particular, $K[x]$ is finite-dimensional and
--   $$
--   \dim_K K[x]=d.
--   $$
--   The family $(x^i)_{0\le i<d}$ is linearly independent over $K$ in the ambient algebra $A$.
--
--   The ambient algebra need not be finite-dimensional, and no restriction is imposed on the characteristic of $K$. Trivial target algebras are included: the hypotheses then force $m=1$, with $d=0$ and the empty power basis. All dimension claims concern the generated subalgebra $K[x]$.
-- source:
--   Derived supporting algebra lemma for the Senthil Kumar mission. At Mathlib revision 0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474, minpoly.unique is in FieldTheory/Minpoly/Field.lean lines 51-60; Algebra.adjoin.powerBasis and its dimension formula are in RingTheory/Adjoin/PowerBasis.lean lines 29-60; PowerBasis.finite, PowerBasis.finrank and linearIndependent_pow are in RingTheory/PowerBasis.lean lines 77, 91-94 and 414-425. Official primary documentation: https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RingTheory/Adjoin/PowerBasis.html , https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/FieldTheory/Minpoly/Field.html#minpoly.unique and https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RingTheory/PowerBasis.html#linearIndependent_pow . For an element x of a commutative K-algebra and a monic m with q(x)=0 iff m divides q, the theorem identifies minpoly_K(x)=m, constructs a power basis of K[x] generated by x, proves finite-dimensionality and dimension deg(m), and proves linear independence of the first deg(m) powers in the ambient algebra. Any field characteristic and trivial target algebras are allowed; the ambient algebra need not be finite-dimensional. No platform dependencies or new definitions.

import Mathlib.RingTheory.Adjoin.PowerBasis

theorem WeierstrassEllipticZeta.monic_evaluation_kernel_power_basis
    (K A : Type*) [Field K] [CommRing A] [Algebra K A]
    (x : A) (m : Polynomial K) (hm : m.Monic)
    (hker : ∀ q : Polynomial K, q.eval₂ (algebraMap K A) x = 0 ↔ m ∣ q) :
    minpoly K x = m ∧
      (∃ b : PowerBasis K (Algebra.adjoin K ({x} : Set A)),
        (b.gen : A) = x ∧ b.dim = m.natDegree) ∧
      FiniteDimensional K (Algebra.adjoin K ({x} : Set A)) ∧
      Module.finrank K (Algebra.adjoin K ({x} : Set A)) = m.natDegree ∧
      LinearIndependent K (fun i : Fin m.natDegree => x ^ (i : ℕ)) := by sorry
